course: dictionary
lesson: 5849
title: Malicious: words that mean harm
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Malicious means wanting to hurt someone, or doing harm on purpose. Look for clue words around it, such as hurt, harm, cruel or on purpose. «Do not help a guilty person by being a malicious witness.» A malicious witness is not trying to tell the truth. They are trying to cause harm, so malicious means meant to do harm.
explain: Malicious can describe a person, a word or an act. A malicious rumour is a story spread to hurt someone. A villain in a book who is cruel on purpose is malicious. The sense is always the same: harm is the aim.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. "Malicious gossip" becomes "gossip meant to hurt someone", and that still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
fact: Malicious means wanting to hurt someone or do harm on purpose.
fact: «Malicious» describes a villain in a story who is cruel on purpose.
fact: Malicious software, called malware, is made to damage a computer or steal information.
fact: A malicious link can harm your computer, so never click one and tell a grown-up if you see one.
fact: The adverb maliciously means in a way that is meant to harm someone.
exercise: «Do not help a guilty person by being a malicious witness.» What does malicious mean here? | Very quiet and shy | *Meaning to harm someone on purpose | Honest and telling the whole truth | Very tired and sleepy
exercise: What does a malicious rumour do? | Makes everyone laugh | *Is meant to hurt or upset someone | Helps a friend feel better | Is always true
exercise: Which link should you never click? | A link to a spelling game from your teacher | *A malicious link that could damage your computer | A link to a library book list | A link to a school photo album
test: A villain in a story is cruel on purpose. Which word best describes the villain? | Cheerful | Happy | Curious | *Malicious
test: Which phrase means gossip meant to hurt someone? | Friendly chat | Happy news | Quiet morning | *Malicious gossip
exam: Malicious software is made to do what to a computer? | *Damage it or steal information | Clean its files for you | Paint its screen | Make it faster
